#!/usr/bin/env bash
cat <<'EOF'
Knowledge Hub Interactive Lab

Lab: Nginx Rate Limiting

Scenario:
  Nginx proxies /api/ correctly, but there is no effective request limit.
  A burst client can overload the backend.

Goal:
  - limit /api/ to 2 requests/second per client IP
  - allow burst=2 without delaying accepted requests
  - return HTTP 429 when the burst budget is exceeded
  - preserve successful proxy traffic to the backend

Workspace:
  /workspace/nginx.conf

Commands:
  status   Show containers and current Nginx config
  check    Send real HTTP traffic and validate throttling behavior
  hint     Show progressively stronger hints
  apply    Recreate the gateway with your edited config
  reset    Restore the intentionally unlimited starter config

Suggested loop:
  status
  check
  nano /workspace/nginx.conf
  apply
  check
EOF
